---
import Network from "../../layouts/Network.astro";
---

<Network
  title="ABF Network — Technology"
  description="Discover ABF Network’s technology infrastructure: web development, broadcasting, content, streaming and digital services."
>
  <section class="network-hero">
    <div class="network-container">
      <p class="network-eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY & INFRASTRUCTURE</p>

      <h1>Technology<br /><span>at the service of the network.</span></h1>

      <p class="network-intro">
        ABF Network develops and operates its own digital infrastructure
        to run its media, services and future projects
        in a coherent and scalable environment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
    <div class="network-container network-two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="network-eyebrow">OUR APPROACH</p>
        <h2 id="architecture-title">Building infrastructure around real-world needs.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="network-copy">
        <p>
          ABF Network technology is not an end in itself.
          It supports the real needs of the media: publishing, broadcasting,
          listening, watching, interacting and developing new services.
        </p>

        <p>
          This approach makes it possible to evolve the
          ecosystem progressively without relying on a fixed architecture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section network-section-dark" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
    <div class="network-container">
      <div class="network-section-heading">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY STACK</p>
        <h2 id="stack-title">An architecture designed for multiple media.</h2>
        <p>
          The different components of the network are developed and integrated
          to work together while retaining their independence.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="network-tech-grid">
        <article class="network-tech-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">01 / WEB</span>
          <h3>Web & Applications</h3>
          <p>
            Modern web interfaces, responsive experiences and applications
            adapted to the needs of different media.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-tech-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">02 / CONTENT</span>
          <h3>Content & CMS</h3>
          <p>
            Editorial content management, publishing and administration
            of information used by the different sites.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-tech-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">03 / BROADCAST</span>
          <h3>Streaming & Broadcast</h3>
          <p>
            Distribution of audio and audiovisual streams and integration
            of the services required for their delivery.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-tech-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">04 / INFRASTRUCTURE</span>
          <h3>Infrastructure</h3>
          <p>
            Services, servers and technical components supporting
            the day-to-day operation of the ecosystem.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-tech-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">05 / MEDIA</span>
          <h3>Audio & Media</h3>
          <p>
            Management of formats, metadata, media identities and
            experiences associated with broadcasting.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-tech-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">06 / DEVELOPMENT</span>
          <h3>Continuous Development</h3>
          <p>
            Regular improvements, new services and progressive
            evolution of the network platforms.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section" aria-labelledby="media-tech-title">
    <div class="network-container network-feature-grid">
      <div class="network-feature-card">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">MEDIA INFRASTRUCTURE</p>
        <h2 id="media-tech-title">A common foundation for different experiences.</h2>
        <p>
          Radio ABF, ABF 2 and future network projects can share certain services
          and technical building blocks while retaining their own identities.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="network-feature-card">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">SCALABILITY</p>
        <h2>An architecture designed to evolve.</h2>
        <p>
          The infrastructure is designed to support the arrival of new
          media, new features and new uses without
          changing the existing foundations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section network-section-dark" aria-labelledby="engineering-title">
    <div class="network-container network-two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="network-eyebrow">ENGINEERING</p>
        <h2 id="engineering-title">Develop rather than simply assemble.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="network-copy">
        <p>
          ABF Network favors an approach where different services
          can be adapted to the specific needs of the network.
        </p>

        <p>
          This approach keeps control of the user experience,
          media identities and platform evolution.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section" aria-labelledby="future-title">
    <div class="network-container">
      <div class="network-feature-card network-next">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">NEXT</p>
        <h2 id="future-title">Technology evolves with the network.</h2>
        <p>
          New services and new media can progressively
          join the ABF Network ecosystem.
        </p>

        <div class="network-next-links">
          <a href="/network/about">The network <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="/network/press">Press <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="/network/partnerships">Partnerships <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Network>

<style>
  .network-hero {
    padding: 112px 0 120px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 82% 18%, rgba(148,163,184,.13), transparent 48%),
      linear-gradient(145deg, #17191e, #090a0c 72%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);
  }

  .network-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    color: #aeb4c0;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .24em;
  }

  .network-hero h1 {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 7.5vw, 104px);
    font-weight: 850;
    line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -.065em;
  }

  .network-hero h1 span {
    color: #aeb4c0;
  }

  .network-intro {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 34px 0 0;
    color: #b8bdc7;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .network-section {
    padding: 96px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
  }

  .network-section-dark {
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #111318, #08090b);
  }

  .network-two-column,
  .network-feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .network-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 760px;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 62px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
  }

  .network-copy {
    max-width: 720px;
    color: #b8bdc7;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .network-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }

  .network-section-heading {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .network-section-heading > p:last-child {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    color: #8f96a3;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .network-tech-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .network-tech-card,
  .network-feature-card {
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.025);
  }

  .network-tech-card {
    min-height: 250px;
    padding: 30px;
  }

  .network-card-index {
    color: #8f96a3;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .18em;
  }

  .network-tech-card h3 {
    margin: 42px 0 12px;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-size: 23px;
  }

  .network-tech-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #969eaa;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .network-feature-card {
    padding: 38px;
  }

  .network-feature-card h2 {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 52px);
  }

  .network-feature-card > p:not(.network-eyebrow) {
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    color: #aeb4c0;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .network-next {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .network-next-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .network-next-links a {
    color: #d8dce3;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .network-next-links a:hover {
    color: #fff;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .network-two-column,
    .network-feature-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 38px;
    }

    .network-tech-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .network-section {
      padding: 72px 0;
    }

    .network-hero {
      padding: 76px 0 84px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .network-tech-card,
    .network-feature-card {
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .network-hero h1 {
      letter-spacing: -.045em;
    }

    .network-next-links {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 14px;
    }
  }
</style>